<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Accessibility Service configuration for Binti.

  FIX #1 — packageNames is intentionally omitted here.
  When set in the XML config it is applied at service LOAD time (before
  onServiceConnected fires), so the service never sees events from packages
  that launch AFTER the initial bind — including DiLink apps that restart
  after a firmware update or a crash.  We set packageNames programmatically
  inside onServiceConnected() in DiLinkAccessibilityService.kt, which is
  the correct and more reliable approach.  Removing it here avoids the
  double-filter that was silently dropping events.

  FIX #2 — typeViewTextChanged and typeViewScrolled are included in
  accessibilityEventTypes. typeViewTextChanged is needed to detect when the
  navigation search field is populated (callContact search flow).
  typeViewScrolled is needed for the recent-calls list scroll in redialLastNumber().

  FIX #3 — flagDefault replaced with explicit flags only. flagDefault is a
  legacy alias that maps to 0 on modern Android and adds nothing.  The three
  explicit flags are what actually matter.  Added flagRequestFilterKeyEvents
  so the service can intercept hardware media keys (needed for endCall
  KEYCODE_ENDCALL dispatch).

  FIX #4 — canRequestFilterKeyEvents capability attribute added.
  flagRequestFilterKeyEvents has no effect unless this capability is also
  declared.  Without it KEYCODE_ENDCALL dispatch in endCall() is silently
  ignored.

  FIX #5 — notificationTimeout reduced from 100 ms to 0.  100 ms means the
  service coalesces/drops events that arrive within 100 ms of each other.
  On a busy DiLink UI (e.g. AC screen animating) this causes window-state
  events to be missed.  0 disables coalescing and delivers every event
  immediately.

  All inline XML comments that previously sat inside the <accessibility-service>
  tag's attribute list have been moved into this top-level comment block.
  XML does not permit comments between attributes of a start tag — AAPT2
  rejects the file with "Element type accessibility-service must be followed
  by either attribute specifications, > or />".
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged|typeViewClicked|typeViewFocused|typeViewTextChanged|typeViewScrolled"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagIncludeNotImportantViews|flagReportViewIds|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows|flagRequestFilterKeyEvents"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canPerformGestures="true"
    android:canRequestFilterKeyEvents="true"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:settingsActivity="com.binti.dilink.MainActivity" />
